---
// Privacy policy (GDPR / DSGVO). Published together with the Impressum.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';
import { legal, legalReady } from '../../lib/legal';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return legalReady ? [{ params: { rest: undefined } }] : [];
}
---
<Base title={`Privacy policy – ${site.name}`} description={`How ${site.name} handles personal data.`}>
  <section class="wrap legal-page">
    <span class="kicker">Datenschutz</span>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This page explains which personal data is processed when you visit this website or get in touch, and what rights you have under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR / DSGVO).</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p><span style="white-space: pre-line">{`${legal.name}\n${legal.address}`}</span><br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></p>

    <h2>Visiting this website</h2>
    <p>This website is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. (USA). When you open a page, your browser sends technical data such as your IP address, the page requested, the date and time, and your browser type. GitHub processes this data to deliver the website and keep it secure. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in a working and secure website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Data may be transferred to the USA; GitHub relies on safeguards recognised under the GDPR for such transfers, such as the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework or standard contractual clauses. More information: <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.</p>
    <p>This website does not use cookies, analytics or tracking tools. Fonts are loaded from this website itself, not from third-party font services.</p>

    <h2>Contact form</h2>
    <p>If you use the contact form, the details you enter (name, email address, type of shoot, preferred date and message) are sent through Formspree, a service of Formspree, Inc. (USA), and forwarded to us by email. We use these details only to answer your enquiry and, if it leads to a commission, to prepare and carry it out. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR (steps prior to entering into a contract) and our legitimate interest in answering enquiries (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Data may be transferred to the USA on the basis of safeguards recognised under the GDPR. More information: <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Formspree Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>If you write to {site.email}, your message and contact details are stored in our mailbox, which is provided by Zoho. We use them only to deal with your request.</p>

    <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
    <p>Enquiries are deleted once they have been dealt with, unless they lead to a commission or statutory retention periods (for example under Austrian tax law) require us to keep them longer.</p>

    <h2>Instagram</h2>
    <p>This website only links to our Instagram profile. No data is sent to Instagram (Meta Platforms) unless you click the link; after that, Instagram's own privacy policy applies.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right to access, rectification, erasure and restriction of processing of your personal data, the right to data portability, and the right to object to processing based on legitimate interests. To exercise these rights, write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    <p>You can also lodge a complaint with the Austrian Data Protection Authority (Österreichische Datenschutzbehörde), Barichgasse 40–42, 1030 Wien, <a href="https://www.dsb.gv.at" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.dsb.gv.at</a>.</p>

    <p style="color: var(--dim); font-size: 14px">Last updated: {legal.privacyUpdated}. · <a href={url('/impressum/')}>Impressum</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
